   "id": "hook",
   "text": "One thousand drones hit Russia overnight. Is the energy truce over?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Russia's defense ministry says it shot down one thousand and fifteen Ukrainian drones over fifteen regions on Sunday. In Saint Petersburg, the governor reports fires at an oil terminal and an oil depot. One person died, five were hurt."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Ukrainian drone maker Fire Point claims its drone hit the terminal. Reports also name a data center of the company VK. A week ago, Trump announced an energy ceasefire. Zelenskyy says Russia has hit Ukrainian energy sites seventy-six times since."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov called the strikes a sign of desperation. He said Russia will respond. NBC News reports that U.S. officials see Washington's easing of Russian diesel sanctions as pressure on Kyiv."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the energy truce survive the winter? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
