  "description": "Russia's defense ministry says it downed 1,015 Ukrainian drones over 15 regions on October 18. St. Petersburg's governor reported fires at an oil terminal and an oil depot, with one person killed and five injured. Ukrainian drone maker Fire Point claims its drone hit the terminal. The strikes came a week after Trump announced an energy ceasefire; Zelenskyy says Russia has struck Ukrainian energy sites 76 times since. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said Russia will respond.\n\nSources:\nCNN: Ukraine defies Trump and launches one of its biggest drone attacks on Russia this year (Oct 18, 2026)\nAP / The Hill: St. Petersburg oil facilities ablaze as Ukraine launches more than 1,000 drones at Russia (Oct 18, 2026)\nABC News: Ukraine targets Russia with more than 1,000 drones, striking oil terminal in St. Petersburg (Oct 18, 2026)\nKyiv Independent: Massive Ukrainian drone attack hit oil facility, bridge, and data center in St. Petersburg (Oct 18, 2026)\nNBC News: Ukraine resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries as anger mounts with Trump (Oct 2026)\n\n#geopolitics #Ukraine #Russia #EnergyCeasefire",
